Setup and Usage
Install the Arduino IDE.
Add ESP32 board support.
Install the Heltec board package.
Open the sketch in the IDE.
Connect the Heltec ESP32 LoRa board and MPU-6050.
Verify the I2C wiring and sensor address.
Upload the code to the board.
Open the serial monitor to inspect telemetry output.
Use a compatible LoRa receiver to collect the packets.

Serial Monitoring
The sketch prints measurements such as:

Roll: 12.34, Pitch: -8.21
and logs when the LoRa transmission completes:
Display Output
The OLED display is used to show the current roll value for quick visual confirmation.

Notes and Limitations
This project is a research prototype and has some limitations:

Hardcoded parameters are used for testing
No robust packet acknowledgment system is implemented
There is minimal error handling
The design is intended for experimentation rather than production deployment
Security and authentication are not included
The code also contains commented sections for Wi‑Fi and UDP communication, indicating that the system was tested or developed in stages for both LoRa and networked forwarding use cases.

Project Status
Status: Prototype / Proof of Concept

